{"name":"Shades of Rhodonite","hex":"#be2bdf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shades","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of shade"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Sunglasses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shades"},{"term":"rhodonite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A manganese inosilicate mineral with some substitution by iron and magnesium, of composition (Mn,Fe,Mg,Ca)SiO3."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhodonite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunglasses","blocks":[{"text":"Sunglasses or sun glasses are a form of protective eyewear designed primarily to prevent bright sunlight and high-energy visible light from damaging or discomforting the eyes. They can sometimes also function as a visual aid, as variously termed spectacles or glasses exist, featuring lenses that are colored, polarized or darkened. In the early 20th century, they were also known as sun cheaters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Allef_Vinicius_2016-10-20_%28Unsplash%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Allef_Vinicius_2016-10-20_%28Unsplash%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunglasses"},{"title":"Rhodonite","blocks":[{"text":"Rhodonite is a manganese inosilicate, with the formula (Mn, Fe, Mg, Ca)SiO3, and member of the pyroxenoid group of minerals, crystallizing in the triclinic system. The term rhodonite was first introduced by Germar. from Ancient Greek  ῥόδον (rhódon) 'rose'. It commonly occurs as cleavable to compact masses with a rose-red color often tending to brown due to surface oxidation. The rose-red hue is caused by the manganese cation (Mn2+)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/8224M-rhodonite3.jpg/330px-8224M-rhodonite3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhodonite"}],"im